{"schema_version":1,"unit_id":"tag:06KC:prose-0002","parent_tag":"06KC","chapter":"formal-defos","node_kind":"paragraph","risk_level":"R2","source_commit":"a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14","source_text":"\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a groupoid in functors on <MATH_0002>.\nTaking completions, we get a quintuple\n<MATH_0003>. By\nRemark <REF_0001>\ncompletion as a functor on <MATH_0004> is a right\nadjoint, so it commutes with limits. In particular, there is a canonical\nisomorphism\n<MATH_0005>\nso <MATH_0006> can be regarded as a functor\n<MATH_0007>. Then\n<MATH_0008>\nis a groupoid in functors on <MATH_0009>, with\nidentity and inverse morphisms being the completions of those of\n<MATH_0010>.\n\n","source_status":"CURRENT","placeholders":{"STRUCT_0001":"\\noindent","MATH_0001":"$(U, R, s, t, c)$","MATH_0002":"$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$","MATH_0003":"$(\\widehat{U}, \\widehat{R}, \\widehat{s}, \\widehat{t}, \\widehat{c})$","REF_0001":"\\ref{remark-completion-restriction-cofset-adjoint}","MATH_0004":"$\\text{CofSet}(\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda)$","MATH_0005":"$$\n\\widehat{R \\times_{s, U, t} R}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\widehat{R} \\times_{\\widehat{s}, \\widehat{U}, \\widehat{t}} \\widehat{R},\n$$","MATH_0006":"$\\widehat{c}$","MATH_0007":"$\\widehat{R} \\times_{\\widehat{s}, \\widehat{U}, \\widehat{t}} \\widehat{R} \\to\n\\widehat{R}$","MATH_0008":"$(\\widehat{U}, \\widehat{R}, \\widehat{s}, \\widehat{t}, \\widehat{c})$","MATH_0009":"$\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda$","MATH_0010":"$(U, R, s, t, c)$"},"render":{"prefix":"","suffix":""},"source_text_hash":"sha256:c437fa4bb5de694795ea95df1e633a581701fe3e1a8d2c8715d64704e7070724","source_structure_hash":"sha256:43d6ea8cc0a7b3978812373f8eca5b2099213e2e1148e366794721646601d191","source_math_hash":"sha256:d54b2a3cb2ce60be60fcd9cec5a085e39bf4b552fa7268aae6932244a4e2bc55"}
